      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm. I feel like the way this is currently doing exception handling is not quite right.\n\nI think we should only use ErrnoException for things that are unlikely in normal execution (ie. should not happen cases), while things like deleting a key that doesn\u0027t exist should throw something more specific.  That makes it easier to catch common errors without catching all of them, while at the same time not requiring one to always check the boolean return code.\n\nboolean for return seems only appropriate for something that would be used in a loop (like getNextKey) and thus basically always tested for...\n\nProbably needs more thought...",
      "revId": "ff5abd342c5304faf67b20b96024e1546c6c2e85",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
